    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d126-a2">

                <pb facs="0312" n="264" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg264"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 194.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Derby to Mr. Pierrepont.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-06-28"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 28,
                        1877</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I referred to the lords of the admiralty
                    your letter of the 8th instant, and. I have now the honor to acquaint you that I
                    am informed that Sir Allen Young has been requested to communicate with your
                    legation as to the transfer to your custody of the relics of the United States
                    steamer Polaris, which were brought home by him from Littleton Island.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>DERBY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwards Pierrepont</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">&amp;c.,&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
